4. Non-obvious edge / Seesaw consequence

The Monid neighbourhood is splitting into two layers:

capability discovery/routing + machine-native purchasing.

Once agents can dynamically discover hundreds/thousands of tools and
purchase them without human API provisioning, integration scarcity
collapses further. The new scarcity is delegated economic authority:
which principal authorized this agent to buy this capability, from
this seller, at this price, with this data, for this purpose?

That means Privately=E2=80=99s authority kernel should treat a paid tool ca=
ll
as one atomic object:

principal -> task grant -> capability -> provider -> data scope ->
quoted cost -> max cost -> payment authorization -> effect -> receipt.

This is stronger than a generic budget counter because it binds money
to purpose and effect.

